        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "If .luarc.json/.emmyluarc.json exist in `test/`, then vim.lsp.config roots the workspace at `test/` , which breaks resolution of `require('test.testutil')` . \r\n\r\nAnd if it does \"work\", then that means `test/` lua code is loaded, so what's the difference?\r\n\r\nAlso, with a `test/` root, that means 2 different luals/emmylua clients (servers?) will be spawned if you open lua files from runtime/ + test/?",
            "created_at": "2026-07-22T11:25:13Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40887#issuecomment-5045206442",
