        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> LuaLS may be loading these and thus slow down LuaLS.\r\n\r\nbtw, i have multiple Nvims open running LuaLS and emmylua, and they all are using a tiny amount of memory (while working properly, unlike before).\r\n\r\nI do see several of the \"unloaded\" buffers as @superatomic noted, but that's harmless, and I don't see why we should \"fix\" that by ignoring directories. If it's a problem then let's find out what the root cause is.",
