        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The test luarc.json added `..` to the library path to make `require(test.util)` work. This meant editing tests was slow (since it loaded everything), but editing `runtime` fast.\n\nIf both servers are running fast then I guess there's no problem. Though I do remember LuaLS took a very long time to load the workspace as it needs to index significantly more files. I doubt that has been fixed.\n\nIf you're the kind of person that has long lived nvim sessions then this probably won't be an issue since you don't init the servers very often. My nvim sessions are very short lived so it probably will be a problem for me.",
